<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n81129" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιβαίνω</span></b> , fut. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βήσομαι</span>: aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιέβην</span>, 
			Ep.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περίβην</span> (v. infr.) :— <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>go round</i>, esp. of one
			defending a fallen comrade, <i>bestride</i> him, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλὰ θέων περίβη καί οἱ σάκος
					ἀμφεκάλυψε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					8.331
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				13.420
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Nic.</u>
				13
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τὰ πίπτοντα σώματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					17.25
				</span></i>
			 : c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιβῆναι ἀδελφειοῦ κταμένοιο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.21
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ τρόπιος βεβαῶτα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					5.130
				</span></i>
			: and c. dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πατρόκλῳ περιβάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					17.80
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				313
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς δὲ κύων . . περὶ σκυλάκεσσι βεβῶσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					20.14
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				1039
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>bestride</i>, as a rider does a horse, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵππον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Pyrrh.</u>
					11
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				2.213e
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς ἵππον</span> Malch.<i><span class="en">
				p.394
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ περιβεβηκότες</span>
			<i>those mounted on</i> the elephants, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				17.88
			</span></i>; of the male camel, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				540a14
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ τὴν ψωλὴν π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				979
			</span></i> (anap.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of
			sound, <i>come round</i> one's ears, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1209
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				Aeol.
			, <i>pass by</i> or <i>beyond</i>, in 
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περβέβαται χρόνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alc.
					<u>Oxy.</u>
					1788
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				15 ii 17
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				p.38
			</span></i> Lobel).</div>
